+# Specification: Subscription Self-Service Management
+
+Users can upgrade, downgrade, change seats, and cancel their subscription from the app without contacting support.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### REQ-001: Enforce role-based permissions
+
+- Account owners and billing admins can change plans, adjust seats, and cancel the subscription.
+- Viewers are read-only and see the current subscription state without action buttons.
+- Cancellation may be performed by any billing admin or the account owner.
+
+### REQ-002: Immediate plan and seat changes
+
+- Upgrades apply immediately with prorated charges.
+- Downgrades apply immediately and the account is credited for unused time.
+- Seat increases apply immediately and are prorated; seat decreases apply at the next renewal.
+
+### REQ-003: Immediate cancellation with refund
+
+- Cancelling ends the subscription immediately and issues a pro-rata refund for the unused portion of the term.
+
+### REQ-004: Price confirmation before charged changes
+
+- Before any change that results in a charge, the user sees the new price, proration amount, and the next renewal total, and must explicitly confirm.
+- Changes that do not produce a charge can be applied without a confirmation step.
+
+### REQ-005: Pending change queue
+
+- Users can queue multiple changes; each is applied in order at the next renewal.
+- The UI shows all queued changes and allows removing them before the renewal date.
+
+### REQ-006: Error surfacing and retry
+
+- If the billing provider rejects a change, the UI shows the provider error message and offers a Retry button.
+- Failed changes remain queued and are retried automatically every 60 seconds until they succeed.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+### AC-001: Viewer read-only access
+
+- Given a signed-in viewer, When they open the subscription page, Then plan, seat, and cancel actions are not available and the current state is displayed.
+
+### AC-002: Immediate upgrade with proration
+
+- Given an account owner on a monthly Starter plan, When they upgrade to Growth mid-cycle, Then the new plan is active immediately and the prorated difference is charged at confirmation.
+
+### AC-003: Immediate downgrade credit
+
+- Given a billing admin on an annual Growth plan, When they downgrade to Starter mid-cycle, Then the plan changes immediately and a credit for unused time is applied.
+
+### AC-004: Immediate cancellation refund
+
+- Given an account owner, When they cancel mid-cycle and confirm, Then the subscription ends immediately and a pro-rata refund is issued to the original payment method.
+
+### AC-005: Price preview before charge
+
+- Given any permitted user, When they select a change that will be charged, Then the exact price impact is displayed before the confirm button can be used.
+
+### AC-006: Multiple queued changes
+
+- Given a permitted user with one queued change, When they queue a second change, Then both appear in the pending list in submission order.
+
+### AC-007: Provider failure retry
+
+- Given the billing provider returns an error during a change, When the error is received, Then the error message is shown in the UI and the change is retried automatically.
